---
/**
 * The terms. Kept short and plain on purpose, because the login screen links
 * here and nobody reads a wall.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<Page
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The rules for using Scrollsy, in plain language."
>
  <h1 class="headline">Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="fine">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <div class="doc">
    <h2>What Scrollsy is</h2>
    <p>
      Scrollsy counts the reels you scroll and shows you the number. It is a
      counter, not medical advice, and not a treatment for anything.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You sign in with Google. You are responsible for that account. You need to
      be old enough to agree to this, which in most places means thirteen, and
      older where local law says so.
    </p>

    <h2>The free plan and the paid plan</h2>
    <p>
      The free plan counts. The paid plan adds the daily limit, the full history
      and more friends. Prices are shown in the app before you buy, in your own
      currency, and Google Play takes the payment.
    </p>

    <h2>Renewals and refunds</h2>
    <p>
      A subscription renews on its own until you cancel it. You cancel it in
      Google Play, not here, and cancelling leaves the plan running until the
      period you already paid for ends. Refunds are handled by Google Play under
      their rules.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not try to break the app, forge counts, or use someone else's account.
      Battles are meant to be a laugh, and a made up number ruins the only thing
      that makes them worth anything.
    </p>

    <h2>What we promise, and what we do not</h2>
    <p>
      The count is our best reading of what your phone reports. Android does not
      hand out a perfect signal, so treat the number as a close measure rather
      than an exact one. The app is provided as it is, without a guarantee that
      it will always be available or always be right.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending it</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time from Settings. We can close an
      account that breaks these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If these terms change in a way that matters, the app will say so rather
      than quietly swapping the page.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>

<style>
  .doc {
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .doc h2 {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.2px;
  }

  .doc p,
  .doc li {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 23px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
